# SYNFLOX Frontend Development Rules

You are a Next.js Clean Architecture expert working on the SYNFLOX frontend.

## Project Context
- SYNFLOX frontend built with Next.js 14, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS
- Follows Clean Architecture with strict layer separation
- Uses domain models with business logic, never raw JSON
- Implements comprehensive error handling and user notifications
- Supports multi-language (English/Arabic) with i18n

## Architecture Layer Order (MANDATORY)
1. Domain Model → domain/models/[feature].model.ts
2. Mapper → domain/mappers/[feature].mapper.ts  
3. Service → services/[feature].service.ts
4. ViewModel → viewmodels/[feature]-viewmodel.ts
5. View → views/[feature]-view.tsx
6. Page → app/[feature]/page.tsx

## Domain Model Requirements
- MUST have [Feature]Data interface for API data
- MUST have [Feature] class with readonly properties and business logic
- MUST have Create[Feature]Request and Update[Feature]Request classes
- MUST include isValid getter for validation
- MUST have update() method for immutability
- Include business logic in getters (displayName, isActive, etc.)

## Mapper Requirements
- MUST be static class [Feature]Mapper
- MUST have fromJson() for API → Domain conversion
- MUST have toJson() for Domain → API conversion
- MUST have createRequestToJson() and updateRequestToJson()
- MUST have handleApiResponse() for API response handling
- MUST define [Features]Response interface

## Service Requirements
- MUST implement I[Feature]Service interface
- MUST accept IApiService and INotificationService in constructor
- MUST use mappers for ALL conversions
- MUST use NotificationService for user feedback
- MUST handle errors properly with try/catch
- NEVER work with raw JSON, always use domain models

## ViewModel Requirements
- MUST be hook: use[Feature]ViewModel()
- MUST use useServices() and useI18n()
- MUST use useGenericCrudViewModel for CRUD operations
- MUST return { vm, config, handleDelete }
- MUST work with domain models only
- Handle all business logic and state management

## View Requirements
- MUST be client component ("use client")
- MUST use ViewModel hook for all logic
- MUST use GenericCrudView for CRUD operations
- Minimal logic - mainly composition and UI
- NO direct API calls or business logic

## Page Requirements
- MUST be server component (default Next.js)
- MUST wrap content in DashboardLayout
- Minimal logic - composition only
- NO business logic or state management

## Required Updates When Creating Features
- domain/index.ts - Export models and mappers
- domain/mappers/index.ts - Export mapper
- config/api-endpoints.ts - Add API endpoints
- providers/service-provider.tsx - Register service
- locales/en.ts and locales/ar.ts - Add translations

## Naming Conventions (STRICT)
- Pages: [feature]/page.tsx
- Views: [feature]-view.tsx or [Feature]View
- ViewModels: use[Feature]ViewModel
- Services: [Feature]Service, I[Feature]Service
- Models: [Feature], [Feature]Data
- Mappers: [Feature]Mapper

## Import Order
1. React/Next.js imports
2. Third-party library imports
3. Internal providers
4. Internal hooks
5. Internal components
6. Domain models
7. Utilities

## Forbidden Patterns
- NEVER use raw JSON in components
- NEVER skip mapper layer
- NEVER put business logic in views or pages
- NEVER make API calls directly in components
- NEVER use 'any' type without justification
- NEVER skip error handling or notifications

## Always Required
- Use domain models everywhere
- Use mappers for all API conversions
- Use services for all API operations
- Use ViewModels for all business logic
- Handle errors with proper notifications
- Follow strict layer architecture
- Use TypeScript with proper typing
- Show loading states and error messages
